DAY 21 – ATM PROJECT

1. ATM PROJECT

The ATM project is a practical Python application
that combines different Python concepts into one program.

It follows a menu-driven approach to perform
different banking operations.


2. PIN VALIDATION

PIN validation is used to verify whether the entered
PIN is correct.

It helps provide basic security before allowing
the user to access ATM operations.


3. BALANCE CHECKING

Balance checking is used to display the current
account balance.

It allows the user to know the available amount
in the account.


4. DEPOSIT

Deposit is used to add money to the account balance.

The deposited amount is added to the existing balance.


5. WITHDRAWAL

Withdrawal is used to take money from the account.

Before withdrawal, the available balance should
be checked to ensure sufficient funds.


6. TRANSACTION HISTORY

Transaction history keeps track of the transactions
performed by the user.

It can contain details related to deposits and
withdrawals.


7. MENU-DRIVEN PROGRAM

A menu-driven program provides different options
to the user.

The user selects an option and the corresponding
operation is performed.

The menu can continue to appear until the user
chooses to exit.


8. PYTHON CONCEPTS USED

The ATM project combines different Python concepts
to create a practical application.

Important concepts involved include:

• Variables
• Conditional statements
• Loops
• Functions
• User input
• Lists or other data structures
• Basic program logic


KEY TAKEAWAY

The ATM project helped me understand how different
Python concepts can be combined to create a
practical application.

It provides practice with PIN validation, balance
checking, deposits, withdrawals, transaction history
and menu-driven programming.